themostseekrit wrote:     tostig wrote:    what compels y'all to choose favorites??  i love them all equally...
    Then you've clearly never done heroin before...  
 It actually really depends on what kind of drug you're talking about. Some drugs can ruin lives, some of them are "okay" provided you use them moderately, and some of them are harmless or completely benign. Also, there is always the argument for a lot of drugs that they can benefit individuals.
 @evilsmile your post oozes of uppers...lay off on them a bit.
 @TheSecAnalyst/PillfirePharmacy PCP doesn't sound like a great idea. It's probably something I'll never come across and I would actually pass on, but my first experience with dissociatives was actually on its 3-methoxy analogue (3-MeO-PCP -- one of the major differences between it and its parent drug is the lack of the mania/insanity component) and it wasn't all too bad. If dissociatives (i.e. DXM, ketamine) are your thing then I'd recommend trying it; some people love it and some hate it.

 @themostseekrit   yes, this weekend has been a bit haywire for me which hasn't happened for quite sometime.  time for some new digital scales i think as that post was epic along with a few others which I am now reflecting on and cringing... on the upside the place is cleaner than its ever been (nothing like being compelled to vacuum at 4am in the morning!)
